00:36:07.610 --> 00:36:10.610
Your trials are not a riddle, Carlisle.

00:36:10.610 --> 00:36:11.610
They are stepping stones.

00:36:11.610 --> 00:36:15.079
on a long path.

00:36:15.079 --> 00:36:17.079
The path that I can blindly walk forever.

00:36:17.079 --> 00:36:21.429
But I understand now, this whole time it's been up to me

00:36:21.429 --> 00:36:24.429
to decide when to take control of my own destiny.

00:36:24.429 --> 00:36:28.429
The trials end when I'm ready for them to end.

00:36:28.429 --> 00:36:30.429
Your journey is far from over.

00:36:30.429 --> 00:36:36.820
But I can only be what the world needs

00:36:36.820 --> 00:36:39.820
when I can finally admit that I'm no longer just the son of Jurel

00:36:39.820 --> 00:36:40.820
or Jonathan Kent.

00:36:40.820 --> 00:36:42.820
And you knew the time would come

00:36:42.820 --> 00:36:45.820
when neither of you could guide me anymore.

00:36:45.820 --> 00:36:46.820
And that time,

00:36:46.820 --> 00:36:48.820
is now.

00:36:48.820 --> 00:36:58.690
Goodbye, Jerome.

00:36:58.690 --> 00:37:57.230
You're all right?

00:37:57.230 --> 00:38:06.630
You know, Clark, walking a mile in your shoes is...

00:38:06.630 --> 00:38:08.630
so different than I imagine it would be.

00:38:08.630 --> 00:38:13.710
When you're just a reporter with a story,

00:38:13.710 --> 00:38:16.710
the word hits the paper, the paper hits the stands, and...

00:38:16.710 --> 00:38:23.889
And it's over.

00:38:23.889 --> 00:38:25.889
But for you, it's...

00:38:25.889 --> 00:38:27.889
It's never over, is it?

00:38:27.889 --> 00:38:41.170
I guess I tell myself there'll always be a balance of good and evil in the world.

00:38:41.170 --> 00:38:43.170
But it's up to me to tip the scale.

00:38:43.170 --> 00:38:47.960
I always knew.

00:38:47.960 --> 00:38:49.960
